Cc: stable <stable@vger.kernel.org> # v4.3+
Patchwork: https://patchwork.linux-mips.org/patch/13164/
Signed-off-by: Ralf Baechle <ralf@linux-mips.org>

Here is the root cause:
The bug arises from the attempt to restore an MSA (MIPS SIMD Architecture) context in a kernel that does not support MSA (i.e., when `CONFIG_CPU_HAS_MSA` is set to `n`). This leads to an overflow of the floating-point register context, causing the restoration process to overwrite adjacent memory areas, specifically the FCSR and MSACSR values. This situation triggers a build error in GCC 6.x due to out-of-bounds array access when trying to set values in the floating-point register context.

